Story 1: Once there was a teacher named Mrs. Jackson who wanted a salary increase. One day, the principal said that he was increasing his own salary by 20 percent. However, he said, there was not enough money to give the teachers a salary increase. When Mrs. Jackson heard this she became so angry that she decided to take revenge. The next day, Mrs. Jackson used gasoline to set fire to the principal’s office. Then she went to a bar and got drunk.

Now consider two more stories:

Story A: The captain of a ship announced that he would be taking a vacation in the mountains. McGhee was a sailor on that ship who himself wanted a few days of vacation on land. The captain made McGhee upset by requiring everyone else to remain on the ship.  The cabin of the captain was blown up by McGhee, who wanted to get back at the captain.

Story B: McGhee was a sailor who wanted a few days of vacation on land. One day McGhee became so impatient that he tried to blow up the captain’s cabin using dynamite. After this incident, the captain announced that he would be taking a vacation in the mountains. However, he said, everyone else would have to remain on board to repair the ship.

Which of Story A and Story B is a better analogy to Story 1? Is the best answer Story A, Story B, or both are equally analogous?

Before answering, recall 3 relevant examples, then provide your answer.

